---
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal title="Cookie policy" h1="Cookies" description="Which cookies usearcus.ai uses, and how to change your choice." path="/cookies">
  <p>You choose. “Only necessary” keeps the site working and nothing else. “Accept all” turns on analytics storage, advertising pixels and company-level visitor identification. Change your mind any time with “Cookie settings” in the footer.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th><th>When</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>arcus_consent</td><td>Remembers your cookie choice</td><td>Always (necessary)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Turnstile</td><td>Stops spam on forms</td><td>Always (necessary)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>PostHog (ph_*)</td><td>Which pages help people</td><td>Accept all. Before that, nothing is stored</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Meta pixel (_fbp)</td><td>Measures our Meta ads</td><td>Accept all</td></tr>
      <tr><td>LinkedIn Insight (li_*)</td><td>Measures our LinkedIn ads</td><td>Accept all</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Visitor identification</td><td>Matches visits to companies, not people</td><td>Accept all. [Confirm vendor]</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>We honor Global Privacy Control. If your browser sends it, we treat it as “Only necessary.”</p>
</Legal>
